comments.body:
Was following an [issue](https://github.com/spesmilo/electrum/issues/8687) and imo it feels a bit stringent to REJECT this. Is leaning towards a warning possible, and let the signer determine how to handle it? So that the function `FindUnsafeSighashType` is only used to detect the unsafe sighash for the sake of emitting a warning

```diff
if (const std::optional<int32_t> sighash{FindUnsafeSighashType(*signer_psbtx)}) {
         const std::string sighash_str{SighashToStr(*sighash)};
-        error = strprintf("Signer used an unsafe sighash type: %s", sighash_str.empty() ? "unknown" : sighash_str);
-        return false;
+        LogWarning("Warning: signer used an unsafe sighash type: %s\n", sighash_str.empty() ? "unknown" : sighash_str);
        // some other action to emit the warning maybe
     }
```

